+aster-brcmfmac is a Rust port of parts of Linux's brcmfmac driver
+(drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211, Linux 6.18): the backplane's
+cores and their resets (chip.c), the PCIe transport and the firmware's
+download (pcie.c), the message rings (msgbuf.c, commonring.c), the NVRAM
+parser (firmware.c), the firmware's commands and events (fwil.c, fweh.c,
+fwil_types.h) and the station's sequence (cfg80211.c, common.c). Linux
+licenses those files under the ISC licence, reproduced below. The port's
+own code is under the MPL-2.0, like the rest of this kernel.
+
+Copyright (c) 2010-2014 Broadcom Corporation
+
+Permission to use, copy, modify, and/or distribute this software for any
+purpose with or without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above
+copyright notice and this permission notice appear in all copies.
+
+THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND THE AUTHOR DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES
+WITH REGARD TO THIS SOFTWARE INCLUDING ALL IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF
+MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY
+SPECIAL, DIRECT, INDIRECT, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES OR ANY DAMAGES
+WHATSOEVER RESULTING FROM LOSS OF USE, DATA OR PROFITS, WHETHER IN AN ACTION
+OF CONTRACT, NEGLIGENCE OR OTHER TORTIOUS ACTION, ARISING OUT OF OR IN
+CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.
+
+The firmware the driver loads (brcm/brcmfmac*-pcie.bin, its .clm_blob and
+NVRAM .txt files) is Broadcom's and Cypress's (Infineon's), from
+linux-firmware, redistributed under its LICENCE.broadcom_bcm43xx and
+LICENCE.cypress files, which the image ships beside the files.
